  "problem": {
    "id": "train-6156",
    "question": "A man drives 60 mph for 3 hours.  How fast would he have to drive over the next 2 hours to get an average speed of 70 mph?",
    "gold": "85",
    "answer": "To have an average speed of 70 mph over 5 hours he needs to travel 70*5=<<70*5=350>>350 miles.\nHe drove 60*3=<<60*3=180>>180 miles in the first 3 hours\nHe needs to travel another 350-180=<<350-180=170>>170 miles over the next 2 hours.\nHis speed needs to be 170/2=<<170/2=85>>85 mph\n#### 85"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the speed the man needs to drive over the next 2 hours to achieve an average speed of 70 mph, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total distance required to achieve an average speed of 70 mph over 5 hours:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total distance} = \\text{Average speed} \\times \\text{Total time} = 70 \\, \\text{mph} \\times 5 \\, \\text{hours} = 350 \\, \\text{miles}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the distance the man has already traveled in the first 3 hours:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance traveled in 3 hours} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 60 \\, \\text{mph} \\times 3 \\, \\text{hours} = 180 \\, \\text{miles}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the remaining distance the man needs to travel in the next 2 hours to reach the total distance of 350 miles:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Remaining distance} = \\text{Total distance} - \\text{Distance traveled in 3 hours} = 350 \\, \\text{miles} - 180 \\, \\text{miles} = 170 \\, \\text{miles}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the required speed for the next 2 hours to cover the remaining 170 miles:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Required speed} = \\frac{\\text{Remaining distance}}{\\text{Time}} = \\frac{170 \\, \\text{miles}}{2 \\, \\text{hours}} = 85 \\, \\text{mph}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the man would have to drive at a speed of \\(\\boxed{85}\\) mph over the next 2 hours to achieve an average speed of 70 mph over the total 5 hours.",
